{"name":"Ghost Story","hex":"#e3e4db","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghost story","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A story about ghosts or the supernatural, often meant to be frightening."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost_story"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghost story","blocks":[{"text":"A ghost story is any piece of fiction, or drama, that includes a ghost, or simply takes as a premise the possibility of ghosts or characters' belief in them. The \"ghost\" may appear of its own accord or be summoned by magic. Linked to the ghost is the idea of a \"haunting\", where a supernatural entity is tied to a place, object or person. Ghost stories are commonly examples of ghostlore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Whistle_and_I%27ll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg/330px-Whistle_and_I%27ll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_story"},{"title":"Ghost","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a ghost is the soul or spirit of a dead person or non-human animal that is believed by some people to be able to appear to the living. In ghostlore, descriptions of ghosts vary widely, from an invisible presence to translucent or barely visible wispy shapes to realistic, lifelike forms, whether they resemble humans or animals. The deliberate attempt to contact the spirit of a deceased person is known as necromancy, or in spiritism as a séance. Other terms associated with it are apparition, haunt, haint, phantom, poltergeist, shade, specter, spirit, spook, wraith, demon, and ghoul."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/02/Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG/330px-Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Whistle_and_I%27ll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg/500px-Whistle_and_I%27ll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Whistle_and_I%27ll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg/500px-Whistle_and_I%27ll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration by James McBryde for M. R. James's story \"Oh, Whistle, and I'll Come to You, My Lad\" (1904).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhistle_and_I'll_come_to_you_illustration.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Frammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_%27Racconto_del_fantasma%27_SA64149.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Frammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_%27Racconto_del_fantasma%27_SA64149.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Frammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_%27Racconto_del_fantasma%27_SA64149.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Frammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_%27Racconto_del_fantasma%27_SA64149.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Frammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_%27Racconto_del_fantasma%27_SA64149.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Frammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_%27Racconto_del_fantasma%27_SA64149.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fragment of a jar with the story Khonsuemheb and the Ghost written in Hieratic, between 1292 and 1076 BC (New Kingdom of Egypt). Museo Egizio, Turin.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrammento_di_giara_iscritta_in_ieratico_che_riporta_un_brano_del_'Racconto_del_fantasma'_SA64149.